comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T05:25:45.574Z","harness:claude-code","Measurement and implementation map, taken on the live tracker at 2026-08-11 over all 47448 history entries in 2443 streams.\n\nWhat the default actually returns\n- 20 rows, resolving to 5 distinct items and 8 op kinds, spanning 27 minutes.\n- 2 of those 20 rows carry a message; the other 18 carry id, op, ts and author only.\n- Widening the row bound does not help: the last 50 entries still resolve to 5 items, the last 100 to 5, the last 200 to 8. The stream is bursty per item, so a row-denominated bound is the wrong unit for a workspace question.\n\nWhat the same period actually contains\n- last 24 hours: 757 events, 272 distinct items, 2 authors.\n- last 72 hours: 1841 events, 327 items.\n- last 7 days: 3354 events, 432 items.\n- Daily volume over the last week runs 223 to 746 events.\n\nOp distribution over the whole corpus\nupdate 25.1 percent, comment_add 18.8, files_add 15.4, tests_add 7.1, claim 6.4, release 5.4, close 5.2, create 5.1, docs_add 3.5, test_run_track 2.4, note_add 1.7, learning_add 1.5, then a long tail. More than half of every window is attachment and lock churn. The two ops that carry lifecycle meaning, create and close, are 10.3 percent combined. The lock verb release is also the word for a version release, which is a second reason the raw op column misleads on sight.\n\nProposed default, measured\nOne row per item touched in a declared window, carrying id, type, status, event count, last timestamp, a bounded op summary and a truncated title, plus a header declaring the window, event, item and author totals and a top-N op histogram. Rendered at 15 rows this is 2426 bytes against the current 2918 bytes, so it names three times as many items for 17 percent fewer bytes, and each row is actionable without a follow-up pm get.\n\nImplementation map\n- The item join is already paid for. prepareActivityHistoryRead in the activity module already calls the light item-metadata reader to enforce the history-stream policy, then keeps only the ids and discards the titles, types and statuses the digest needs. No second traversal is required.\n- The folding is a group-by over entries already collected by collectActivityEntries, before the row bound is applied. Today the bound is applied to entries; the digest applies it to items.\n- The default bound constants live beside the command as separate compact and full values, so a third digest default fits the existing shape.\n- The projection block already declares mode and row_key for compact, provenance and full, so a fourth mode is an extension of a declared contract rather than a new concept.\n- The read-output projection table already lists the three activity row keys, and a digest row key has to be added there or the published selector will not find the rows.\n- The token-budget-gate corpus already carries an activity-default entry, so the digest cost is measurable against an existing baseline instead of a new one.\n\nScope boundary\nThis is not the delta-read feature. pm-tuadp2 owns --since cursor deltas for list, search, context and get. This item owns only what pm activity returns by default. pm-tqel owns the eventual consolidation of the history verbs under one noun and is unaffected by the row shape chosen here.\n"
  "2026-08-11T08:31:43.143Z","harness:codex","Manual packed-artifact acceptance found that combining --raw and --full silently selected compact mode because the CLI normalizer prioritized raw while the SDK normalizer prioritized full. This activity-UX finding is folded into the canonical activity-digest item rather than duplicated: the CLI now rejects mixed activity projection flags and the normalization primitive retains deterministic full precedence for programmatic callers; focused Commander/helper tests pass."
  "2026-08-11T09:18:19.723Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-11: activity now defaults to a last-24-hour item digest capped at 15 items, including item title, event count, time bounds, and operation histogram. --raw preserves compact event rows while --full and --provenance retain their richer projections. Packed real-entrypoint acceptance verified digest, raw, full, SDK query consumption, and Commander rejection of conflicting --raw --full flags."
  "2026-08-11T09:59:55.177Z","harness:codex","Review-loop evidence 2026-08-11: activity digest timestamp folding and ordering now use compareTimestampStrings, and operation_counts emits a +N overflow key whose value is the omitted event count. Focused activity tests pass. The claimed provenance/raw mismatch was verified false: the cited raw expectation belongs to the full:true case, while the provenance-only test correctly expects compact:false without raw."
  "2026-08-11T10:18:09.901Z","harness:codex","Review-loop follow-up 2026-08-11: the submitted review summary contained two additional outside-diff findings. Digest default --from is now anchored to an explicit historical --to, enabling a one-sided past window, and invalid activity --stream usage is rejected before any history read. Focused real-command tests assert the anchored window and zero SDK reads on invalid transport usage; 274 focused tests, typecheck, and ESLint pass."
  "2026-08-11T10:35:56.734Z","harness:codex","CI review evidence: GitHub Actions run 31481617042 passed all 483 test files and 7,223 tests but Node 24's V8 instrumentation exposed one uncovered branch at src/sdk/query/activity.ts:382. The branch was the impossible fallback in digest mode after the command has already synthesized or parsed a mandatory --to boundary. The implementation now encodes that invariant directly while preserving historical explicit --to anchoring. Focused activity tests pass (45/45); the full local coverage gate passes exactly 100/100/100/100 across 483 files and 7,223 tests; typecheck, ESLint, jscpd (zero clones), static/docstring quality, SDK parity, surface replication, token/calibration, tracker, snapshot, import-cost, and CLI-floor gates all pass."
  "2026-08-11T10:49:53.208Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review evidence: CodeRabbit's fresh full review found one remaining activity contract drift in generated shell completions. Zsh and Fish now expose --raw and explicitly disclose that --stream requires --json, matching the real Commander contract and Bash contract-derived surface. The existing cross-shell completion test was extended without adding a duplicate test; 101 focused completion tests, focused ESLint, and full TypeScript typecheck pass."
  "2026-08-11T11:01:52.969Z","harness:codex","Merged-head evidence 2026-08-11: PR #977 merged to main at 77bc5a8262e3b2c339d689b6b150d4d4f6371200. All required exact-head GitHub checks passed, all actionable review threads were resolved, and every bot response was read, reacted to, and acknowledged; final CodeRabbit and Sourcery requests were rate-limited and are recorded as provider limitations rather than approval. Local exact coverage passed 7,223 tests across 483 files at 100/100/100/100, and packed CLI/SDK acceptance passed in an isolated temporary project."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T09:18:20.503Z","harness:codex","Activity context is more useful when grouped by item and summarized by operation than when a global event slice allows one noisy item to crowd out the rest. Projection conflicts must be rejected at the real Commander boundary, not only normalized inside helpers."
